#
# Counter-example for math:ProbabilityValueRangeShape (Rule P1): a math:ProbabilityValue
# whose math:quantityValue magnitude (1.5) lies ABOVE the closed unit interval [0, 1].
# Single violation: the range gate on math:quantityValue fires — shacl.MaxInclusiveConstraintComponent
# (math:ProbabilityOutOfBounds). It carries a gmeow:hasReferenceFrame so the framing gate
# math:ProbabilityValueFramedShape (P3) stays SATISFIED, it is not typed math:OddsValue /
# math:LogOddsValue so math:ProbabilityScaleDisjointShape (P2) stays satisfied, and it
# carries no logic:confidence so math:ConfidenceAsProbabilityConstraint (P10) stays silent —
# so EXACTLY ONE finding is raised and NO sibling probability shape also fires.
# Back-reference: math:ProbabilityValue / math:ProbabilityOutOfBounds (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecProbabilityValueAboveUnitBad).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:aboveUnitProbability a math:ProbabilityValue ;
    math:quantityValue "1.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
    gmeow:hasReferenceFrame ex:forecastFrame .

ex:forecastFrame a gmeow:ReferenceFrame .
<http://example.org/math/aboveUnitProbability> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasDimension> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/dimensionless> .
